# Project standards

- Never hardcode tokens, API keys, or Discord IDs. Every config value flows through `src/config/env.ts`.
- Never commit `.env`, `data/`, `*.db`, cookies, or `TODO.md`.
- No `any`, no non-null `!`, no `as` casts outside zod / boundary parse sites.
- Validate all external JSON (Discord payloads you reshape, Apex API, Spotify) with zod.
- User-facing failures throw `UserFacingError`. Never leak stack traces or secrets into Discord replies.
- Prefer `readonly` fields and explicit return types on public module surfaces.
- Keep modules self-contained under `src/modules/<name>/` with an `index.ts` that exports a `Module`.
